#[doc = "# Server and delivery foundation\n\nStatus: Done\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M0\n\n## User value\nRun and document a minimal server before implementing domain features.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given the server starts with no database, GET /health returns HTTP 200 and exactly ok plus a newline; unknown routes return 404.\n2. Given `MEALSHOP_LISTEN_ADDR` is set to a valid socket address, the server binds there; an invalid address or occupied port exits with an error.\n3. Given a main commit, CI verifies formatting, clippy, tests, debug/release artifacts, coverage, declared MSRV, dependency licences/advisories, SPDX SBOM and binary-size metrics.\n4. Given docs publication, requirements, specs, ADRs and Rust API documentation are browsable on Pages; Renovate uses the existing `RENOVATE_TOKEN`.\n5. Given bootstrap delivery, source and AGPL text are on main and each workflow has been run and its outcome checked.\n\n## Out of scope\nProduct endpoints, authentication, persistent data and Flutter.\n\n## UX notes\nNo product UI in the bootstrap.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F01](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Verification: [bootstrap evidence](../page_docs_bootstrap_verification_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0001_bootstrap_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0001_bootstrap_adrs_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0001_bootstrap_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Decisions for ingredient catalogue and nutrition\n\n- [ADR 0002](../page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md/index.html): preserve quantity dimensions,\n  provenance and unknowns; perform no implicit volume/mass conversions.\n\n## Feature-local decisions\n2026-11-07 (Proposal, reversible within this slice):\n- Use bounded scaled integers (six decimal places) and checked rational arithmetic through\n  final display rounding. JSON amounts are strings; original decimal spelling is retained.\n  `serde`/`serde_json` (MIT OR Apache-2.0) provide typed API\n  serialization already present transitively; declare them directly now that they are used.\n- Retain a fixed per-100-g edible-portion basis and a named nutrient registry with explicit\n  units; serving counts are positive integers. F03 will extend user-facing quantity units.\n- Read a validated immutable catalogue at startup, using bundled public-domain/CC0 USDA SR\n  Legacy snapshots by default. An optional local JSON file replaces the whole catalogue.\n  This does not decide the persistent household storage architecture of F18.\n- A stateless estimate endpoint takes ingredient IDs/grams/servings/context and returns\n  complete or explicitly partial totals, retained provenance and preparation warnings.\n- Supply a minimal same-origin browser workbench instead of starting the full Flutter shell.\n  Only public operator-provided catalogue records are readable; no user data is persisted.\n- Reviewed educational notes carry source, applicability and limitations separately from\n  measured composition. No dose/benefit is inferred when component data is absent.\n\nProvider curation/refresh, a complete nutrient vocabulary and general cooking-retention models\nremain future refinements. The starter catalogue is deliberately small, not an authoritative\nfood/allergen database. Customer authorization to start F02 is not acceptance of a finished PR.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# Plan for ingredient catalogue and nutrition\n\n## Affected modules\n`src/quantities.rs`: validated decimal amounts and gram quantities.\n`src/nutrition/`: catalogue model/validation and pure nutrient calculation.\n`src/api.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `src/main.rs`: read-only catalogue and stateless calculation HTTP API.\n`src/web/`: browser workbench. `data/`: reviewed catalogue and original source snapshots.\n`tests/`: acceptance checks and fixtures. No new crate or storage abstraction.\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Refine acceptance/UX notes and record implementation proposals before implementation.\n- [x] Define failing acceptance tests for provenance, scaling, missing data and education (AC 1–4, 5–9).\n- [x] Implement typed decimal quantities, validated catalogue, pure aggregation and rounding (AC 1–3, 6–9).\n- [x] Freeze and verify primary-source starter records and evidence notes (AC 1, 4).\n- [x] Expose read-only/search/detail API, stateless calculations and startup catalogue loading (AC 5–9).\n- [x] Build and exercise the browser workbench including errors/unknowns (AC 3, 10).\n- [x] Run quality/security/MSRV checks and prepare the reviewable feature branch/demo.\n\n## Validation\nDerive black-box HTTP tests from this specification before implementing the handlers. Check\nsource-record preservation, known arithmetic/portion scaling, exact decimal behaviour and\nrounding boundaries; distinguish partial/unknown from zero; reject invalid/oversized input.\nVerify the bundled values directly against the frozen USDA source records, not copied assertions.\nExercise custom-catalogue startup validation and existing health/startup regression tests.\nBrowser-check normal, unknown/partial, error and narrow-screen flows. Run the repository gate,\nMSRV and CI; record exact outcomes before marking implementation review-ready.\n\n## Evidence\nSee [validation.md](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_validation_md/index.html) and [the demo guide](../page_docs_guides_nutrition_md/index.html).\n\n## Acceptance\n- [x] Customer merged [PR #4](https://github.com/Th3Link/mealshop/pull/4) and confirmed acceptance (2026-11-07).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Ingredient catalogue and nutrition\n\nStatus: Done (PR #4 merged; customer confirmed 2026-11-07)\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nUnderstand the ingredients used in recipes, with trustworthy nutritional context.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given an ingredient, its identity, aliases, edible form (raw/cooked), nutrient basis, source, version and uncertainty are retained.\n2. Given known composition and quantities, energy, macros and micronutrients are calculated per recipe and per serving with explicit units and rounding.\n3. Given missing nutrient values or cooking/yield uncertainty, the UI distinguishes unknown values from zero and explains the calculation limits.\n4. Given beta-glucan in oats or soluble fibre in psyllium husks/chia, educational notes reference evidence, applicable quantities and limitations without promising health outcomes.\n\n## Demo classification (customer clarification, 2026-11-07)\nThe browser surface is a pure pragmatic demo for testing, not the Nextcloud or standalone\nproduct UI. See F21/F22 and ADR 0007. Significant product design work belongs in the\nproduct-client workflow, with a dedicated UX/UI agent when the customer requests one.\n\n## Delivery contract (2026-11-07)\nThe customer authorized F02 implementation. The first slice provides a read-only ingredient\ncatalogue, a stateless calculation API and a browser nutrition workbench at `/`.\nA reviewed bundled catalogue uses frozen USDA SR Legacy oats/chia records and an explicitly\nunknown psyllium-husk composition. A local JSON catalogue may replace it at startup; it is\nnot a household database or a storage adapter. No remote lookup occurs during app use.\n\n5. `GET /api/ingredients` supports name/alias search; detail lookup retains ingredient ID,\n   form, per-100-g edible-portion basis, source record/version/licence and uncertainty.\n6. `POST /api/nutrition/calculate` accepts ingredient IDs, positive decimal-string grams,\n   positive integer servings and preparation context. Decimal inputs have up to six fractional\n   digits and a maximum of 1,000,000,000; at most 100 lines and 1,000,000 servings are accepted.\n   Quantities never pass through binary floating point. Results round half away from zero to\n   two decimal places only after aggregation and portion scaling, with units and policy stated.\n7. Missing/null values produce null recipe/portion totals plus explicitly labelled known\n   subtotals and missing ingredient IDs; a measured zero remains a complete zero. No nutrient\n   is inferred from another (in particular no beta-glucan estimate from total fibre).\n8. Input-source uncertainty and preparation context accompany every result. Unmodelled cooking\n   displays a warning: no retention, water/yield or cooking-loss correction has been applied.\n9. Invalid IDs, unsupported units/fields, zero/negative/nonfinite/exponent/numeric JSON amounts,\n   excessive input and malformed catalogue files fail explicitly; calculations do not mutate data.\n10. The browser allows ingredient selection, gram quantities and serving count; prominent\n    per-serving macros, a nutrient table, unknown/partial states, source links and evidence notes\n    remain usable on narrow screens and with keyboard navigation. Errors preserve user input.\n\n## Out of scope\nInvented nutrient values or medical treatment recommendations. General unit conversion/preferences (F03),\nrecipe storage (F04/F18), household/authentication (F09), provider auto-sync and Flutter (F18).\n\n## UX notes\nSee [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_ux_notes_md/index.html); the browser workbench is an end-to-end review surface for this slice.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F02](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_adrs_md/index.html). Validation: [validation.md](../page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_validation_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Nutrition workbench UX\n\nScope: disposable, pragmatic test demo only. This is not the Nextcloud or standalone product\nweb UI (F22); do not invest in a design system here. Flutter remains F18.\n\n- Header identifies Mealshop and the ingredient/nutrition workbench, with a short limits notice.\n- Ingredient search filters by canonical name and aliases. Detail shows form, basis, source,\n  version, uncertainty and evidence conditions; missing values show “Unknown”, never 0.\n- Recipe input uses labelled native controls for ingredient, grams, integer servings and\n  preparation context; adding/removing ingredients is keyboard-accessible. No auto-save.\n- Calculate is explicit. Controls disable only while a request is pending. Errors use a live\n  region and retain the entered recipe; replacing results clears stale data on errors.\n- Per-serving energy, protein, carbohydrate and fat appear prominently. A full table compares\n  recipe/portion values and units. Partial rows label known subtotals and name missing ingredients.\n- Source uncertainty and unmodelled cooking are shown next to results; education never asserts\n  a dose is met without measured component data. Source links open safely as HTTPS links.\n- Narrow screens stack controls/cards; tables scroll within their own container. Use semantic\n  headings, native buttons/labels, visible focus, readable contrast and status text beyond colour.\n- Empty catalogues show a clear message; failed requests offer retry without destroying input.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_ux_notes_md {}

#[doc = "# F02 validation\n\nDate: 2026-11-07. Status: implementation verified locally; customer acceptance pending.\n\n## Acceptance traceability\n| Criteria | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| AC 1, 5 | `catalogue_search_and_detail_retain_provenance_and_evidence`; original USDA snapshots; source verifier |\n| AC 2, 6 | `recipe_and_serving_values_are_scaled_from_source_values`; exact portion/rounding tests |\n| AC 3, 7–8 | `unknown_and_partial_values_are_never_reported_as_complete_zero`; browser partial/preparation flow |\n| AC 4 | evidence conditions/limitations checked in catalogue/detail test and browser notebook/results |\n| AC 6, 9 | bounds/repeated-line tests; invalid payloads; custom catalogue, duplicate keys and startup validation |\n| AC 10 | normal calculation, partial/unknown, invalid grams preserving input and 390 px responsive view exercised in browser |\n\nThe first five API acceptance tests were run against the bootstrap before handlers existed\nand failed as expected. They pass with the implementation; the suite now has 15 tests total.\n\n## Local gate results\n- `python3 scripts/generate_docs.py --check`: PASS.\n- `python3 scripts/verify_catalogue.py`: PASS, 26 values match frozen USDA responses exactly.\n- `node --check src/web/app.js`: PASS.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`: PASS.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --locked`: 15 passed, 0 skipped.\n- `cargo build --release --locked`: PASS.\n- `cargo deny check licenses`: PASS.\n- `cargo audit`: PASS, no advisory ignores.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked`: PASS.\n- `cargo msrv verify -- cargo check --all-targets --locked`: PASS, Rust 1.85.0.\n\n## Browser observations\n- 100 g oats + 25 g chia, two servings: 255.25 kcal and 10.51 g protein per serving.\n- Switching to psyllium leaves totals unknown and labels the known subtotals separately.\n- Unmodelled cooking shows the lack of retention/yield correction.\n- Negative gram input shows an error, preserves the input and hides stale results.\n- At a 390 px viewport the document has no horizontal overflow; controls and the two-column\n  macro-card layout are readable. The full nutrient table scrolls within its own wrapper.\n- Source/evidence notes remain separate from measured component values; beta-glucan and\n  soluble fibre remain unknown, never extrapolated from total fibre.\n\n## Review scope and remaining work\nThis PR provides read-only public reference data, calculations and a browser review surface.\nA local JSON file can replace the catalogue; startup validation is not a persistence adapter.\nThere are no stored recipes, household records, general unit preferences or Flutter shell.\nThe 15-definition vocabulary is a starter subset, not exhaustive micronutrient coverage.\nSource refresh, further verified foods and cooking-retention models require later work.\nF02 stays In progress until customer review/acceptance. GitHub CI outcomes are checked on the\nfeature PR and reported with the delivery, not inferred from local test success.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0002_ingredients_nutrition_validation_md {}

