#[doc = "# Federated recipe and meal-plan exchange\n\nStatus: Draft\nPriority: Could\nOrigin: Customer\nMilestone: M5\n\n## User value\nExchange selected content between independent Mealshop servers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. Given opt-in federation, a user can share an authorized recipe between servers without opening private household data.\n2. Given a shared meal-plan template for similar intolerances, sharing uses explicit consent and minimal disclosed attributes, never raw health profiles by default.\n3. Given imported recipes, the exchanged representation contains the original source link only.\n4. Given an untrusted remote server, authentication, protocol versioning, moderation, revocation limitations and abuse controls are specified and tested before enablement.\n\n## Out of scope\nA federation protocol choice or automatic cross-server health-profile discovery.\n\n## UX notes\nUI flows, accessibility, empty/error states and user review points must be specified before Ready.\n\n## Links\nRequirement: [F20](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html). Delivery tasks: [plan.md](../page_specs_0020_federation_plan_md/index.html). Decisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0020_federation_adrs_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0020_federation_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Decisions for internationalization\n\n- [ADR 0007](../page_docs_adr_0007_localization_and_web_clients_md/index.html): de/en first; demo vs product boundary.\n- [ADR 0002](../page_docs_adr_0002_quantities_and_nutrition_md/index.html): preserve exact amounts and unit meanings.\n\n## Slice-local proposals\nUse a small framework-free ES module for demo-only resources and pure locale helpers, with\nNode's built-in test runner. No JavaScript dependencies or production i18n framework are chosen.\nScope starter ingredient translations by source record identity, not a possibly colliding\noperator-defined ingredient ID. Untranslated data keeps its source wording and attribution.\nCanonical HTTP decimal strings remain dot-separated; only the presentation boundary uses commas.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_adrs_md {}

#[doc = "# Plan for internationalization\n\n## Current slice\n- [x] Record customer direction and distinguish demo scope from production clients.\n- [x] Add keyed de/en demo resources, starter ingredient labels and original-text fallback (AC 1–2).\n- [x] Add exact decimal entry/display and preserve inputs during language changes (AC 3, 5).\n- [x] Add stable warning codes and focused locale/API checks (AC 5–6).\n- [x] Verify repository gate and prepare a reviewable PR.\n\n## Remaining product work\n- [ ] Specify versioned content translations and API locale negotiation (AC 2, 5).\n- [ ] Integrate localization across Vue/Nextcloud, standalone web and Flutter (AC 4).\n- [ ] Complete locale-aware date/plural/error contracts across those clients (AC 4–6).\n\n## Validation\nUse pure locale tests for supported regional tags, dictionary coverage/fallback, source-name\nfallback, localized search and precise decimal strings beyond JavaScript's safe integer range.\nRetain Rust nutrition tests; add a warning-code contract test. Exercise German entry with a\ncomma and language switching without changing the canonical recipe. Reuse the existing demo\nlayout and do not add visual design work.\n\n## Delivery evidence (2026-11-07)\nSee [shared validation](../page_specs_0023_kitchen_ingredient_catalogue_validation_md/index.html). The current slice\nis implemented; cross-client localization and customer acceptance remain open.\n\nCustomer accepted the initial demo/catalogue slice by merging PR #5. Broader product work remains open.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_plan_md {}

#[doc = "# Internationalization and localized content\n\nStatus: In progress\nPriority: Must\nOrigin: Customer (after PR #4 merge, 2026-11-07)\nMilestone: M1\n\n## User value\nUse Mealshop in German or English, find ingredients by familiar names, and enter precise\nquantities in a familiar notation without changing their meaning.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. UI messages are keyed resources with German/English support, an explicit language choice,\n   regional-tag normalization and a documented fallback. Missing translations never render keys.\n2. Ingredient, recipe and educational content have language-independent identities and\n   reviewed, versioned translations. Search covers localized names, aliases and source names;\n   unavailable translations show source text with a clear original-language label.\n3. Quantity input accepts the active locale's decimal separator without binary floating point\n   or guessing grouped numbers; formatting uses locale separators while retaining exact values.\n   Locale changes preserve valid input and do not silently reinterpret invalid input.\n4. Number/date/plural formatting and messages work in Vue/Nextcloud, standalone web and Flutter\n   clients. Locale settings are independent of preferred units and serving quantities.\n5. API IDs, nutrient meanings/units and stored canonical decimal strings remain stable.\n   Localizable errors/warnings use stable codes plus parameters, not parsing of English prose.\n6. Translation coverage, fallback, locale switching, search and exact decimal boundaries have\n   focused checks; nutrition calculations and original source provenance are unchanged.\n\n## Current slice\nOnly the disposable nutrition demo gets de/en UI resources, language selection (saved locally\nwhen browser storage is available), browser-language detection, localized starter names/forms,\nmultilingual demo search and exact decimal entry/output. Reviewed content absent from the demo\ntranslation catalogue is explicitly presented in its original language. Calculation warnings\nget additive stable codes so the demo does not translate backend sentences by string matching.\nThis is a first step, not completion of all six cross-client criteria.\n\n## Out of scope for this slice\nA production translation service, account-wide language preferences, complete ingredient/recipe\ncontent translation storage, API content negotiation, all backend error codes, Vue/Flutter clients\nand additional languages. Preserve source facts instead of generating unreviewed health translations.\n\n## UX notes\nSee [ux-notes.md](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_ux_notes_md/index.html). Keep the demo pragmatic; do not add product design work.\n\n## Links\nRequirements: N09/N10 in [requirements](../page_docs_requirements_md/index.html).\nDecisions: [adrs.md](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_adrs_md/index.html). Work: [plan.md](../page_specs_0021_internationalization_plan_md/index.html).\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_specification_md {}

#[doc = "# Demo localization UX\n\n- A visible language selector offers Deutsch and English. Initial preference: saved choice,\n  otherwise the browser language (de variants map to German, unsupported languages to English).\n- All demo controls/statuses have keyed messages. German ingredient names are shown for reviewed\n  starter record identities; custom/unknown records use their original names without guessed translations.\n- Search matches localized labels, canonical names and aliases in both supported languages.\n- German gram input uses a comma, English a dot; no grouping separators are accepted in inputs.\n  Outputs may group digits. Switching language preserves exact values and results; invalid\n  fields keep their text and require correction rather than being reinterpreted in the new locale.\n- Original-language provenance, uncertainty and education are labelled explicitly. Missing\n  translations must not hide limitations or imply content has been reviewed in German.\n- Header/title/footer say Demo; replace marketing copy with a pragmatic explanation. No redesign.\n"]
pub mod page_specs_0021_internationalization_ux_notes_md {}

